The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
static void start_split_transaction_timeout(struct fw_transaction *t, struct fw_card *card)
{
	if (list_empty(&t->link) || WARN_ON(t->is_split_transaction))
		return;
	t->is_split_transaction = true;
	scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &card->split_timeout.lock)
		delta = card->split_timeout.jiffies;
	mod_timer(&t->split_timeout_timer, jiffies + delta);
}
```
```c
	scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &card->split_timeout.lock) {
		t->split_timeout_cycle =
			compute_split_timeout_timestamp(card, packet->timestamp) & 0xffff;
	}
	start_split_transaction_timeout(t, card); // called without card->transactions.lock
```
Reason:
The original `start_split_transaction_timeout` function modifies the transaction list (via `list_empty` and `is_split_transaction`) and starts a timer without holding `card->transactions.lock`. This allows concurrent enumeration or modification of the transaction list (e.g., during AR response handling) to race with this code, causing data corruption or use-after-free.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
static void start_split_transaction_timeout(struct fw_transaction *t, unsigned int delta)
{
	if (list_empty(&t->link) || WARN_ON(t->is_split_transaction))
		return;
	t->is_split_transaction = true;
	mod_timer(&t->split_timeout_timer, jiffies + delta);
}
```
```c
		scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &card->split_timeout.lock) {
			t->split_timeout_cycle =
				compute_split_timeout_timestamp(card, packet->timestamp) & 0xffff;
			delta = card->split_timeout.jiffies;
		}
		scoped_guard(spinlock_irqsave, &card->transactions.lock)
			start_split_transaction_timeout(t, delta);
```
Reason:
The fix moves the acquisition of `card->transactions.lock` into the caller, ensuring that `start_split_transaction_timeout` (which manipulates the transaction list) is executed while holding that lock. The split-timeout lock is still used to safely read `delta`, but the critical section for the transaction list is now properly protected, eliminating the race condition.

